# =============================================================================
# Auth — LOGIN requests (VS Code REST Client)
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend (http://localhost:4000).
#   2. Run requests top-to-bottom — request 1 creates the Ada user the rest
#      of the file depends on.
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE. These are manual probes; the automated suite is in
#     src/test/java.
#   - Expected codes: 200 ok, 400 invalid payload, 401 bad credentials,
#     423 locked (app.security.lockout: 5 fails / 15 min), 429 rate limited
#     (20 logins/min per IP — see the comment near the bottom).
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: register Ada (201 on first run, 409 if she already exists — both fine)
# Expected: 201 or 409 — either way the account exists for the requests below
POST {{baseUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada Obi",
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234567"
}

### 2 — Valid login
# Expected: 200 — accessToken, refreshToken, message, user
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3 — Wrong password
# Expected: 401 — generic invalid-credentials (no hint about which part failed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}

### 4 — Unknown email (also: response should cost the same ~Argon2 time as #3)
# Expected: 401 — same generic error and roughly the same latency as #3
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ghost.user@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 5 — Invalid email format
# Expected: 400 — "Please provide a valid email address"
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 6 — Missing email field
# Expected: 400 — "Email is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — Blank password
# Expected: 400 — "Password is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": ""
}

### 8 — Password below the 8-char minimum
# Expected: 400 — "Password must be between 8 and 128 characters"
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.obi@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Pass1!"
}

### 9 — Empty JSON body
# Expected: 400 — both NotBlank constraints violated
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 10 — Setup: register Bola (lockout test persona)
# Expected: 201 or 409 — account exists for the lockout flow below
POST {{baseUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Ade",
  "email": "bola.ade@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348055551234"
}

### 11 — Wrong password for Bola — SEND THIS 5 TIMES IN A ROW
# Expected: 401 on every send — each failure counts toward the lockout
# (app.security.lockout.max-attempts = 5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.ade@devtunde.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}

### 12 — Correct password for Bola AFTER 5 failures
# Expected: 423 — account locked. A correct password does not unlock it.
# Unlock happens automatically after 15 minutes (lock-duration).
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.ade@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limit (no live request — it would poison the shared per-IP bucket):
# sending ANY 21 login requests within one minute from the same IP returns
# 429 + Retry-After: 60 on the 21st (app.security.rate-limit.limit = 20).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
